      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Marais%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Ojibwe called the harbor Gichi-biitoobiig, meaning “great duplicate water,” a nod to the two bays that form its harbor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Marais%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Gunflint Trail, a National Scenic Byway, starts in Grand Marais and winds northwest toward the Ontario border.",
